# Generated. `node build.mjs` reproduces it in seconds, and it carries ~14MB of
# the practice's photography - the repo rules forbid committing binary/media.
dist/

# Verification screenshots of the rebuild. Regenerated on demand by shot.mjs.
shots/
slices/

# Regenerated by weigh.mjs from dist/; it is a measurement, not a source.
weight-report.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   content/, content-db/  - the extracted copy. Text, small, and the only
#                            record of what the compromised host published.
#   build-report.json      - names the links that were unwrapped and why.

# The node graphs fetched back out of the container - 6.6 MB, and regenerated
# by `ship-payload.mjs -> run-convert.mjs -> fetch-nodes.mjs` whenever the
# pages change. The parent practice's workflow makes the same call.
#
# NOT ignored: instatic-media-map.json. It is small, and it is the only record
# of which upload each local file became - Instatic assigns the id, so the map
# cannot be recomputed from dist/ alone, only re-read off the live site.
converted-pages.json
